GG use Berlin embryo Hackers spikesTo practice our CSS skills, let's try to make a CSS-only layout that works for older browsers and still supports modern devices!

Take a look at the following layout:
```
<div class="container">
  <div class="main-content">
    <header>Header</header>
    <main>Main Content</main>
    <footer>Footer</footer>
  </div>
  <div class="sidebar">
    <nav>Navigation</nav>
    <aside>Aside</aside>
  </div>
</div>
```
To make it work for older browsers, we'll use the following techniques:

*   Using float for the sidebar
*   Harnessing vertical stretching for modern screens

Here's the CSS code:

```css
.container {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  padding-left: 240px;
}

.main-content {
  display: block;
  padding: 20px;
  margin: 100px auto;
  width: 80%;
}

.main-content header,
.main-content main,
.main-content footer {
  display: block;
  text-align: center;
}

/* For older browsers with support for IE 5+, Mozilla Firefox 1.x, Safari 1.x, etc */
.main-content nav {
  float: left;
}

.second-sidebar {
  float: right;
}

/* Hijack main container to accommodate vertical stretching */
.main-content {
  width: 90vw;
  padding-left: 150px;
}
```

